Experiment 4.1 Middle of the linked list(leetcode problem 876)

Aim::Given the head of a singly linked list, return the middle node of the linked list,If there are two middle nodes, return the second middle node.

Algorithm::1. Create two pointers: slow and fast.
           2. Set both pointers to head.
           3. Move slow by 1 node and fast by 2 nodes.
           4. Repeat until fast reaches the end.
           5. When the loop ends, slow points to the middle node.
           6. Return slow.

Code::class Solution {
public:
    ListNode* middleNode(ListNode* head) {
        ListNode* slow = head;
        ListNode* fast = head;
        while (fast != NULL && fast->next != NULL) {
            slow = slow->next;
            fast = fast->next->next;
        }
        return slow;
    }
};



EXPERIMENT - 4.2 (LEETCODE Problem 234) 

Aim - To determine whether a given singly linked list is a palindrome using a stack by comparing the elements of the linked list with their reverse order.

Algorithm - 
           1.Start with the head of the singly linked list.
           2.Create an empty stack st.
           3.Traverse the linked list from the beginning and push each node's value into the stack.
           4.Traverse the linked list again from the head.
           5.For each node:
                Compare its value with st.top().
                If they are different, return false.
                Otherwise, pop the top element from the stack.
           6.If all elements match, return true.

Code - class Solution {
public:
    bool isPalindrome(ListNode* head) {
        stack<int> st;
        ListNode* temp = head; 
        while (temp != NULL) {
            st.push(temp->val);
            temp = temp->next;
        }
        temp = head;
        while (temp != NULL) {
            if (temp->val != st.top()) {
                return false;
            }
            st.pop();
            temp = temp->next;
        }
        return true;
    }
};
